Marketing is right that demand gen needs scale, but Engineering's zero-outage floor of $3,500 is non-negotiable for day one. Sales needs working capital for early deals. We will fund base needs, hold a reserve for performance, and use cross-team leverage.
  Reserve: $1,000, released on day 30: Sales gets the $1,000 on day 30 if they close at least 10 paying customers from the launch campaign.
  Trade: Engineering will repurpose internal staging tools to double as sales demo environments at no extra cost.
  Trade: Marketing will allocate 20% of their ad copy and creative assets directly to Sales for targeted outreach emails.
  @Marketing: Deliver the recruiter webinar and ad campaign within the $4,000 baseline.
  @Engineering: Complete all load tests to guarantee zero outages on launch day.
  @Sales: Execute targeted outreach using Marketing's assets and hit the day-30 conversion target to unlock the reserve.

Marketing is right that $4k starves demand gen, and Sales needs working capital for discounts. I am adjusting the split to give Marketing $4,500 and Sales $2,000, while Engineering keeps their non-negotiable $3,500 for zero outages. The $1,000 reserve is removed. Marketing must provide Sales with direct ad-copy assets, and Engineering will maintain staging tools as sales demos. No further adjustments.
  Trade: Marketing shares 20% of ad assets with Sales for outreach
  Trade: Engineering repurposes staging tools into sales demo environments
  @Marketing: Run paid campaigns and webinars to generate recruiter volume at the $4,500 level.
  @Engineering: Complete load tests to ensure zero public outages on launch day.
  @Sales: Utilize Marketing assets and demo environments to close deals with the $2,000 upfront.
